* =====================================================================================================
* usb_input__smf5v0a.lib  -  SMF5.0A 200 W unidirectional TVS (SOD-123FL), base board D1 (VBUS -> GND)
* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Part      : Littelfuse SMF5.0A (MPN on the base netlist; LCSC C151296)
* Datasheet : Littelfuse "TVS Diodes Surface Mount - 200W > SMF Series", Revised 06/07/17
*             https://www.littelfuse.com/assetdocs/tvs-diodes-smf-datasheet  (LCSC mirror C151296)
* Cross-ref : Vishay SMF5V0A..SMF58A datasheet Rev. 2.4, 04-Jul-2023, doc 85881
*             https://www.vishay.com/doc?85881  (same SOD-123FL / DO-219AB die family)
* Vendor model: no Littelfuse SMF SPICE model could be obtained (product page refuses scripted
*             access). Vishay's family library
*             https://www.vishay.com/docs/86542/spice_vishay_smf5v0a-to-smf58a.zip (rev 24.09.2024)
*             contains NO SMF5V0A entry (first entry is SMF6V0A), so this is a datasheet fit. From the
*             Vishay family models it takes the exponential reverse-leakage shape (their N = 13 reverse
*             diode), the CJ shape (M = 0.39, VJ = 0.92 of SMF6V0A) and the unheated RS (0.02 ohm).
*             Breakdown is an offset forward diode instead of SPICE BV (BV did not converge under the
*             0.8 ns IEC 61000-4-2 edge).
*
* Modelled (Littelfuse table "Electrical Characteristics", TA = 25 C, unless noted):
*   VBR      6.40 V min / 7.00 V max at IT = 10 mA          -> param vbr (default 6.70 = mid)
*   VC       9.2 V max at IPP = 21.7 A (10/1000 us)          -> param rd: rd = (9.2 - 7.0)/21.7 = 0.101 ohm
*            makes the vbr = 7.00 corner meet VC (model: vbr 6.995 + rd 0.0924 gives VBR(10 mA) 7.00 V,
*            VC 9.19 V; heating included = worst case).
*            Fast (ns..us) pulses see the unheated die: Vishay family model RS = 0.02 ohm -> rd = 0.02.
*   IR       400 uA max at VR = 5.0 V (Littelfuse; Vishay: 5 uA max) -> param ilk = leakage at 5.0 V,
*            nlk = its emission coefficient (Vishay family: 13). For ilk = 400u, nlk = 22 keeps the
*            leakage at 6.40 V below 5 mA so the VBR min (6.40 V at 10 mA) entry still holds.
*   VF       forward: Littelfuse Fig. 7 (IF 0.01 A @ 0.72 V, 10 A @ ~1.5 V, 25 A @ ~2.65 V)
*            -> IS = 9.7e-12, N = 1.34, RS = 0.066 ohm
*   CJ       Littelfuse Fig. 6: ~800 pF at VR = 0 V for VBR = 6.4 V (Vishay table 1120 pF typ);
*            the lower Littelfuse value is used (less charge absorbed = conservative for ESD).
*   IPP 21.7 A (10/1000 us), PPPM 200 W, IEC 61000-4-2 30 kV contact: ratings, checked in the tests.
*
* NOT modelled:
*   - VBR and IR temperature coefficients (given in neither datasheet; Vishay's family models carry no
*     TBV1), so breakdown and leakage are temperature-independent. VF follows the SPICE default IS(T) law
*     (Littelfuse Fig. 5 shows VF falling ~1.5 mV/C, which the default EG/XTI reproduces to first order).
*   - knee shape below IT: ~60 mV/decade (Vishay family: NBV 0.5, i.e. ~30 mV/decade); V(1 mA) is ~60 mV
*     below VBR(10 mA)
*   - self-heating during long pulses (rd corner 0.0924 ohm bounds it), package/lead inductance (the
*     tests add layout inductance explicitly), turn-on delay (DS: < 1 ns from 0 V to VBR min).
*
* Pins: K = cathode (pin 1, VBUS on the base board), A = anode (pin 2, GND).
* Corners used by the tests: typ (vbr 6.70, rd 0.02), clamp-max (vbr 6.995, rd 0.0924),
*                            clamp-min/leak-max (vbr 6.42, rd 0.02, ilk 400u, nlk 22): with the
*                            400 uA leakage this still gives V(10 mA) >= 6.40 V (VBR min).
* =====================================================================================================
.subckt USBIN_SMF5V0A K A params: vbr=6.70 rd=0.02 ilk=5u nlk=13 cj0=800p
* forward conduction (anode -> cathode), Littelfuse Fig. 7 fit, junction capacitance Fig. 6
Dfwd  A K USBIN_SMF5V0A_DF
* reverse breakdown as a forward diode behind a (vbr - 0.5956 V) offset: V(K,A) = vbr at IT = 10 mA, ~60 mV/decade
* knee, rd above it. (SPICE BV breakdown did not converge under the 0.8 ns IEC edge.) EG = Vf(10 mA), XTI = 0 makes
* the knee temperature-independent (no VBR temperature coefficient is specified).
Dbrk  K kz USBIN_SMF5V0A_DZ
Vbrk  kz A {vbr-0.5956}
* soft reverse leakage, exponential like the Vishay family's reverse high-N diode (slope 1/(nlk*25.9 mV)),
* = ilk at 5.0 V, zero at 0 V; written as a B source so that it carries NO temperature dependence (none is
* specified; a SPICE diode would make it fall with temperature through Vt, which is unphysical). The exponent
* is soft-limited at 5 (x148) so it stays bounded far into breakdown, where Dbrk carries the current anyway.
Blk   K A I=ilk*(exp(5*tanh((v(K,A)-5.0)/(5*nlk*0.025865)))-exp(5*tanh(-5.0/(5*nlk*0.025865))))
.model USBIN_SMF5V0A_DF D(IS=9.7e-12 N=1.34 RS=0.066 CJO={cj0} M=0.39 VJ=0.92 TT=0)
.model USBIN_SMF5V0A_DZ D(IS=1e-12 N=1 RS={rd} CJO=0 EG=0.5956 XTI=0)
.ends USBIN_SMF5V0A
